. These are draft importance estimates for role requirements, not learner aptitude scores; SME review required."}, "big5_assessment": {"traits": ["Conscientiousness", "Openness", "Emotional Stability"], "rationale": "Curiosity finds anomalies while systematic checking keeps analytical conclusions traceable. Trait-demand ratings are provisional role descriptors, not personality diagnosis or exclusion criteria."}, "work_values_assessment": {"values": ["Impact", "Autonomy", "Creativity"], "rationale": "The role offers analytical problem solving and evidence-based environmental impact, not regulatory authority. Work-value ratings are provisional career-exploration descriptors, not employment or pay guarantees."}}, "embedding_text": "ROLE\nName: Environmental Data Analyst\n\nCAREER CONTEXT\nIndustry: Water Resources, Environment and Public Utilities\nDomain: Environmental Data and Analysis\nRole Family: Environmental Data Analytics\n\nROLE SUMMARY\nEnvironmental Data Analyst supports convert measurements into findings in the RAREMINDS River Mission workplace case. May analyse and report source-backed patterns; cannot certify laboratory methods, infer a proven source without evidence or authorise corrective actions.\n\nWORK CONTEXT\nL3 source import, join, comparison, dashboard and findings → L5 analyst-route portfolio. Inputs: six accepted sample IDs, field and laboratory source tables, campaign dates, DO/BOD comparisons and missing-key exceptions. Course-wide foundations: CAP01, CAP02, CAP06, CAP07, CAP08, CAP11. Role focus: CAP05, CAP06. May analyse and report source-backed patterns; cannot certify laboratory methods, infer a proven source without evidence or authorise corrective actions.\n\nTYPICAL WORK ACTIVITIES\nEnvironmental Data Analyst: Import records and verify data types, keys and source IDs; Join laboratory and field evidence on exact sample ID; Clean data, calculate station and campaign differences and flag anomalies; Build chart/filter views and record interpretation limits. When source evidence is missing, record a HOLD/exception and identify the reviewing owner.\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACTIONS\nImport records and verify data types, keys and source IDs; Join laboratory and field evidence on exact sample ID; Clean data, calculate station and campaign differences and flag anomalies; Build chart/filter views and record interpretation limits; Check each saved record against source ID, units, errors and role authority.\n\nDELIVERABLES & OUTPUTS\nSource-backed outputs: Clean, joined and traceable analysis table; Data exception and reconciliation log; Comparative Excel dashboard with filters; Qualified analytical findings and source-backed handover. Associated capability evidence: CAP01 Investigation brief; CAP02 Stakeholder and site register; CAP05 Laboratory comparison sheet; CAP06 Validated analytical workbook; CAP07 Evidence and hypothesis matrix; CAP08 Criteria comparison and gap report; CAP11 Final professional investigation portfolio.\n\nINTEREST AND WORK-STYLE ALIGNMENT\nICR (Investigative/Conventional/Realistic): I supports investigating anomalies; C supports accurate datasets and repeatable formulas; R reflects the use of quantitative monitoring instruments and evidence. Proposed role-environment orientation, not an individual assessment.\n\nAPTITUDE ALIGNMENT\nKey areas: Data Interpretation, Logical Reasoning, Numerical Reasoning\nReadiness: Exact-key joins, calculations, charts and QA checks require strong numeric and data reasoning. These are draft importance estimates for role requirements, not learner aptitude scores; SME review required.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL ALIGNMENT\nKey traits: Conscientiousness, Openness, Emotional Stability\nWork style: Curiosity finds anomalies while systematic checking keeps analytical conclusions traceable. Trait-demand ratings are provisional role descriptors, not personality diagnosis or exclusion criteria.\n\nWORK-VALUE ALIGNMENT\nKey values: Impact, Autonomy, Creativity\nMotivation: The role offers analytical problem solving and evidence-based environmental impact, not regulatory authority. Work-value ratings are provisional career-exploration descriptors, not employment or pay guarantees.\n\nEDUCATION AND ELIGIBILITY\nGate: Preferred\nStreams: B.Sc. Environmental Science; B.Sc. Biotechnology; B.Sc. Geography; B.Sc. Geology; B.Tech Computer Science Engineering; B.Tech Information Technology; BCA; MCA; B.Sc. Statistics; B.Sc. Mathematics; B.Sc. Data Science; B.Sc. Artificial Intelligence; Geoinformatics / Remote Sensing; Public Health programmes\n"}'::jsonb;
 i uuid; d uuid; f uuid; roleid uuid; scopeid uuid; familyid uuid; contextid uuid; existing jsonb;
BEGIN

 i:=pg_temp.river_entity('industries',r->>'industry_code',r->>'industry_name','081cf05d-7a89-5c4a-897f-bde339d91318'::uuid);
