"], "rationale": "Cross-check monitoring evidence, compare methods and requirements and write precise escalation notes. These are draft importance estimates for role requirements, not learner aptitude scores; SME review required."}, "big5_assessment": {"traits": ["Conscientiousness", "Emotional Stability", "Agreeableness"], "rationale": "Documentation accuracy and calm evidence-based escalation are essential where conclusions may affect people. Trait-demand ratings are provisional role descriptors, not personality diagnosis or exclusion criteria."}, "work_values_assessment": {"values": ["Impact", "Security", "Autonomy"], "rationale": "The work rewards traceability, responsibility and public impact; decisions belong to authorised compliance reviewers. Work-value ratings are provisional career-exploration descriptors, not employment or pay guarantees."}}, "embedding_text": "ROLE\nName: Environmental Compliance Support Associate\n\nCAREER CONTEXT\nIndustry: Water Resources, Environment and Public Utilities\nDomain: Environmental Compliance and Public Programmes\nRole Family: Environmental Compliance Evidence\n\nROLE SUMMARY\nEnvironmental Compliance Support Associate supports track evidence against applicable requirements in the RAREMINDS River Mission workplace case. May prepare compliance evidence and flag deficiencies; cannot issue regulatory clearance, certify drinking-water safety or sign statutory compliance conclusions.\n\nWORK CONTEXT\nL2 method/QC evidence → L3 criteria checks → L4 approval boundaries → L5 compliance-route portfolio. Inputs: monitoring register, method-verification fields, laboratory evidence, relevant reference criteria, approval and exception logs. Course-wide foundations: CAP01, CAP02, CAP06, CAP07, CAP08, CAP11. Role focus: CAP05, CAP08, CAP10. May prepare compliance evidence and flag deficiencies; cannot issue regulatory clearance, certify drinking-water safety or sign statutory compliance conclusions. Support-only degree pathways listed in source: B.Com, BA LLB, LLB.\n\nTYPICAL WORK ACTIVITIES\nEnvironmental Compliance Support Associate: Compile monitoring, laboratory and method records with source IDs; Compare the correct parameter, test method, unit and criteria; Track evidence gaps, conditional approvals and reviewer status; Escalate unsupported compliance or safety claims. When source evidence is missing, record a HOLD/exception and identify the reviewing owner.\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACTIONS\nCompile monitoring, laboratory and method records with source IDs; Compare the correct parameter, test method, unit and criteria; Track evidence gaps, conditional approvals and reviewer status; Escalate unsupported compliance or safety claims; Check each saved record against source ID, units, errors and role authority.\n\nDELIVERABLES & OUTPUTS\nSource-backed outputs: Monitoring and compliance evidence register; Methods-and-criteria comparison sheet; Gap and escalation register; Qualified compliance-support handover. Associated capability evidence: CAP01 Investigation brief; CAP02 Stakeholder and site register; CAP05 Laboratory comparison sheet; CAP06 Validated analytical workbook; CAP07 Evidence and hypothesis matrix; CAP08 Criteria comparison and gap report; CAP10 Project action pack; CAP11 Final professional investigation portfolio.\n\nINTEREST AND WORK-STYLE ALIGNMENT\nCIR (Conventional/Investigative/Realistic): C fits structured records and requirements; I fits method and criteria interpretation; R reflects measurement-based site evidence. Proposed role-environment orientation, not an individual assessment.\n\nAPTITUDE ALIGNMENT\nKey areas: Data Interpretation, Logical Reasoning, Verbal Reasoning\nReadiness: Cross-check monitoring evidence, compare methods and requirements and write precise escalation notes. These are draft importance estimates for role requirements, not learner aptitude scores; SME review required.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL ALIGNMENT\nKey traits: Conscientiousness, Emotional Stability, Agreeableness\nWork style: Documentation accuracy and calm evidence-based escalation are essential where conclusions may affect people. Trait-demand ratings are provisional role descriptors, not personality diagnosis or exclusion criteria.\n\nWORK-VALUE ALIGNMENT\nKey values: Impact, Security, Autonomy\nMotivation: The work rewards traceability, responsibility and public impact; decisions belong to authorised compliance reviewers. Work-value ratings are provisional career-exploration descriptors, not employment or pay guarantees.\n\nEDUCATION AND ELIGIBILITY\nGate: Preferred\nStreams: B.Sc. Chemistry; B.Sc. Environmental Science; B.Sc. Microbiology; B.Tech Civil Engineering; B.Tech Environmental Engineering; B.Tech Chemical Engineering; B.Com; BA Public Administration; BA Political Science; LLB; BA LLB\n"}'::jsonb;
